message.content:
Fuel injectors for diesel engines are classified in heading 8409 as parts suitable for use solely or principally with compression-ignition internal combustion piston engines. Marine diesel engines fall under 8408.10, so parts go in 8409.99 or 8409.91. Heading 8409.91 covers parts for spark-ignition engines, and 8409.99 covers other parts. The 8409.99 statistical suffixes include 8409.99.91 (other) and 8409.99.9190 for "Other". Both subheadings cover non-spark parts, and 8409.99.91 has further breakouts such as 8409.99.9130 for fuel injection pumps or nozzles.

Bosch injector 0432191581 is a nozzle holder assembly. CBP rulings have classified fuel injectors for diesel engines under 8409.99.9190 (other), after earlier use of 8409.99.9130. I recall the HTS 8409.99.91 subdivisions: 8409.99.9130 is "Fuel injection pumps," 8409.99.9150 is "Cylinder liners," 8409.99.9160 is "Pistons," and 8409.99.9190 is "Other". I'm not confident fuel injectors have their own breakout, so I'll go with 8409.99.9190.

{"hts_code": "8409.99.9190", "reason": "A fuel injector used in marine diesel (compression-ignition) engines is a part suitable for use solely or principally with engines of heading 8408, so it falls under 8409.99 as an other part."}
